[2026-03-14T20:44:55.785Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V3UEYGxrFFJpZqUrAKXoao","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# AirbnbClone Test Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Page: Login / Register (`/login`)\n     4→\n     5→<!-- Components: LoginForm, RegisterForm, AuthToggle -->\n     6→\n     7→### Component: AuthToggle\n     8→\n     9→#### Test: Auth page defaults to login mode\n    10→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/login` for the first time (not logged in).\n    11→- **Expected:** The page displays in login mode with the email input field visible, a \"Log In\" submit button, and a toggle link reading \"Don't have an account? Register\" at the bottom.\n    12→\n    13→#### Test: Toggle from login to register mode\n    14→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    15→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Don't have an account? Register\" link.\n    16→- **Expected:** The form switches to register mode showing name and email fields, a \"Register\" submit button, and the toggle link changes to \"Already have an account? Log In\".\n    17→\n    18→#### Test: Toggle from register back to login mode\n    19→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    20→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Already have an account? Log In\" link.\n    21→- **Expected:** The form switches back to login mode with only the email field and \"Log In\" button visible.\n    22→\n    23→#### Test: Toggle preserves no stale input between modes\n    24→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    25→- **Action:** User types \"test@example.com\" in the email field, then toggles to register mode.\n    26→- **Expected:** The register form fields are empty (no carried-over email value).\n    27→\n    28→### Component: LoginForm\n    29→\n    30→#### Test: Login with valid email redirects to home\n    31→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode. A user with email \"guest@example.com\" exists in the database.\n    32→- **Action:** User types \"guest@example.com\" in the email input and clicks the \"Log In\" button.\n    33→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/auth` with the email, stores the returned user object in Redux state, and redirects to the home page (`/`).\n    34→\n    35→#### Test: Login with empty email shows validation error\n    36→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    37→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Log In\" button without entering an email.\n    38→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Email is required\"). No API call is made.\n    39→\n    40→#### Test: Login with invalid email format shows validation error\n    41→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    42→- **Action:** User types \"not-an-email\" in the email field and clicks \"Log In\".\n    43→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). No API call is made.\n    44→\n    45→#### Test: Login with non-existent email shows error\n    46→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode. No user with email \"unknown@example.com\" exists.\n    47→- **Action:** User types \"unknown@example.com\" and clicks \"Log In\".\n    48→- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"No account found with this email\"). The user remains on the login page.\n    49→\n    50→#### Test: Login form email input is functional on repeated use\n    51→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    52→- **Action:** User types \"wrong@example.com\", submits and gets an error, then clears the field, types \"guest@example.com\", and clicks \"Log In\" again.\n    53→- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is logged in and redirected to home.\n    54→\n    55→### Component: RegisterForm\n    56→\n    57→#### Test: Register with valid name and email creates account and redirects to home\n    58→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode. No user with email \"newuser@example.com\" exists.\n    59→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field and \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    60→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/auth` with name and email, stores the returned user object in Redux state, and redirects to the home page (`/`).\n    61→\n    62→#### Test: Register with empty name shows validation error\n    63→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    64→- **Action:** User types \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field but leaves the name field empty, then clicks \"Register\".\n    65→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Name is required\"). No API call is made.\n    66→\n    67→#### Test: Register with empty email shows validation error\n    68→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    69→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field but leaves the email field empty, then clicks \"Register\".\n    70→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Email is required\"). No API call is made.\n    71→\n    72→#### Test: Register with invalid email format shows validation error\n    73→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    74→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field and \"bad-email\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    75→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). No API call is made.\n    76→\n    77→#### Test: Register with already-existing email shows error\n    78→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode. A user with email \"existing@example.com\" already exists.\n    79→- **Action:** User types \"Some Name\" in the name field and \"existing@example.com\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    80→- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"An account with this email already exists\"). The user remains on the register form.\n    81→\n    82→#### Test: Register form fields are functional on repeated use\n    83→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    84→- **Action:** User fills in name and an already-existing email, submits and gets an error, then changes the email to a new unique email and clicks \"Register\" again.\n    85→- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is registered and redirected to home.\n    86→\n    87→## Page: Home / Search (`/`)\n    88→\n    89→<!-- Components: SearchBar, CategoryFilter, PropertyGrid, PropertyCard, FavoriteButton, FiltersPanel, Pagination -->\n    90→\n    91→### Component: SearchBar\n    92→\n    93→#### Test: Search bar displays all input fields on load\n    94→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n    95→- **Expected:** The search bar is visible at the top of the page containing four inputs: a location text input with placeholder \"Where are you going?\", a check-in date picker, a check-out date picker, and a guest count selector. A search/submit button with a magnifying glass icon is visible.\n    96→\n    97→#### Test: Search by location filters property results\n    98→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist in \"Paris\", \"New York\", and \"Tokyo\".\n    99→- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" into the location input and clicks the search button.\n   100→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where the city matches \"Paris\". Properties in other cities are not displayed.\n   101→\n   102→#### Test: Search by check-in and check-out dates filters results\n   103→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Some properties have bookings that overlap with the selected dates.\n   104→- **Action:** User selects a check-in date of \"2026-04-01\" and a check-out date of \"2026-04-05\" using the date pickers, then clicks the search button.\n   105→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that are available (not fully booked) for the selected date range. The date pickers display the selected dates in a readable format.\n   106→\n   107→#### Test: Search by guest count filters results\n   108→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist with max_guests values of 2, 4, and 8.\n   109→- **Action:** User sets the guest count to 5 and clicks the search button.\n   110→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where max_guests >= 5. Properties with fewer guest capacity are hidden.\n   111→\n   112→#### Test: Combined search with all fields filters results\n   113→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Multiple properties exist with varying locations, availability, and guest capacities.\n   114→- **Action:** User types \"New York\" in the location field, selects check-in \"2026-05-10\" and check-out \"2026-05-15\", sets guests to 3, and clicks the search button.\n   115→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties in New York that are available for those dates and accommodate at least 3 guests.\n   116→\n   117→#### Test: Clearing search fields and re-searching shows all results\n   118→- **Initial state:** User has performed a search for \"Paris\" and the grid shows filtered results.\n   119→- **Action:** User clears the location field (making it empty) and clicks the search button.\n   120→- **Expected:** The property grid resets to show all properties (unfiltered by location).\n   121→\n   122→#### Test: Search bar is functional on repeated use\n   123→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   124→- **Action:** User searches for \"Paris\", views results, then clears the location field, types \"Tokyo\", and searches again.\n   125→- **Expected:** The first search shows only Paris properties. After the second search, the grid updates to show only Tokyo properties. The location input correctly reflects \"Tokyo\".\n   126→\n   127→#### Test: Check-in date picker prevents selecting past dates\n   128→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   129→- **Action:** User opens the check-in date picker.\n   130→- **Expected:** Dates before today are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected.\n   131→\n   132→#### Test: Check-out date must be after check-in date\n   133→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page and has selected a check-in date of \"2026-04-10\".\n   134→- **Action:** User opens the check-out date picker.\n   135→- **Expected:** Dates on or before \"2026-04-10\" are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected. Only dates after the check-in date are selectable.\n   136→\n   137→#### Test: Guest count selector enforces minimum of 1\n   138→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   139→- **Action:** User interacts with the guest count selector.\n   140→- **Expected:** The minimum selectable value is 1. The user cannot set the guest count to 0 or a negative number.\n   141→\n   142→### Component: CategoryFilter\n   143→\n   144→#### Test: Category filter bar displays all property type chips\n   145→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   146→- **Expected:** A horizontal scrollable bar of category chips is displayed below the search bar. Chips are shown for each property type: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". No chip is selected by default (all properties are shown).\n   147→\n   148→#### Test: Clicking a category chip filters properties by that type\n   149→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of various types exist (apartments, houses, cabins, etc.).\n   150→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   151→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes visually selected/highlighted (e.g., bold outline or filled background). The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Cabin\".\n   152→\n   153→#### Test: Clicking the selected category chip deselects it and shows all properties\n   154→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip currently selected.\n   155→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip again.\n   156→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip returns to its unselected appearance. The property grid shows all properties again (no category filter applied).\n   157→\n   158→#### Test: Switching between category chips updates the filter\n   159→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip selected, showing only cabin properties.\n   160→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Villa\" chip.\n   161→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes unselected and the \"Villa\" chip becomes selected/highlighted. The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Villa\".\n   162→\n   163→#### Test: Category filter works in combination with search bar\n   164→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist: a cabin in Paris, an apartment in Paris, and a cabin in Tokyo.\n   165→- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" in the search bar location field and clicks search, then clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   166→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only cabin properties in Paris. Both the search and category filters are applied simultaneously.\n   167→\n   168→#### Test: Category filter bar is horizontally scrollable when chips overflow\n   169→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page on a narrow viewport where all chips don't fit in one row.\n   170→- **Expected:** The category filter bar is horizontally scrollable. The user can scroll left/right to see all property type chips.\n   171→\n   172→#### Test: Category chip is functional on repeated use\n   173→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   174→- **Action:** User clicks \"Apartment\" (filtered), then clicks \"House\" (switches filter), then clicks \"House\" again (deselects), then clicks \"Cabin\" (filtered again).\n   175→- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected chip and the property grid filters. The final state shows only cabin properties with the \"Cabin\" chip highlighted.\n   176→\n   177→### Component: PropertyGrid\n   178→\n   179→#### Test: Property grid displays properties in a responsive grid layout\n   180→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Multiple properties exist in the database.\n   181→- **Expected:** Properties are displayed in a responsive grid: 1 column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3-4 columns on desktop. Each property is rendered as a PropertyCard.\n   182→\n   183→#### Test: Property grid shows message when no properties match filters\n   184→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   185→- **Action:** User searches for a location with no matching properties (e.g., \"Atlantis\").\n   186→- **Expected:** The property grid area displays a \"No properties found\" message instead of an empty grid. The message suggests adjusting filters or search criteria.\n   187→\n   188→#### Test: Property grid loads and displays properties from API on initial page load\n   189→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Properties exist in the database.\n   190→- **Expected:** The grid fetches properties via `GET /api/properties` and displays property cards. While loading, a loading indicator is shown. Once loaded, the property cards appear with correct data.\n   191→\n   192→### Component: PropertyCard\n   193→\n   194→#### Test: Property card displays all required information\n   195→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with title \"Cozy Cabin\", city \"Aspen\", country \"US\", property_type \"Cabin\", price_per_night 150, an average rating of 4.5, and 12 reviews.\n   196→- **Expected:** The property card shows: the main property image at the top, a \"Cabin\" property type badge, the title \"Cozy Cabin\", location \"Aspen, US\", \"$150 / night\" price, and a star icon with \"4.5 (12 reviews)\" rating display.\n   197→\n   198→#### Test: Property card shows property image\n   199→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with at least one image (the first image by display_order).\n   200→- **Expected:** The property card displays the main image (lowest display_order) at the top of the card with rounded top corners. If no image exists, a placeholder image is shown."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BYZBEUEUZFsy2s9VeJe4VB","session_id":"bf64fb1f-6d22-482a-898e-953cd6c2617e","uuid":"4a9048bb-629c-47fd-8c61-065220227b6b"}
