[2026-03-14T20:45:03.373Z] {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HsFt81pQ7XaCrUupiNR2zC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RfkRTwt6r42PMtAf1eCxYA","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/repo/apps/AirbnbClone/docs/tests.md","offset":600,"limit":400},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9277,"cache_read_input_tokens":35124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9277,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BYZBEUEUZFsy2s9VeJe4VB","session_id":"bf64fb1f-6d22-482a-898e-953cd6c2617e","uuid":"63660731-7dfd-4a24-a11a-a1d2e5525da0"}
[2026-03-14T20:45:03.584Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RfkRTwt6r42PMtAf1eCxYA","type":"tool_result","content":"   600→## Page: My Trips (`/trips`)\n   601→\n   602→<!-- Components: TripsTabs, TripCard, CancelBookingDialog -->\n   603→\n   604→### Component: TripsTabs\n   605→\n   606→#### Test: My Trips page requires login\n   607→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in.\n   608→- **Action:** User navigates to `/trips`.\n   609→- **Expected:** The user is redirected to the login page (`/login`). The My Trips page content is not displayed.\n   610→\n   611→#### Test: My Trips page defaults to Upcoming tab\n   612→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and navigates to `/trips`.\n   613→- **Expected:** The page displays three tabs: \"Upcoming\", \"Past\", and \"Cancelled\". The \"Upcoming\" tab is selected/highlighted by default. The content area shows upcoming trips (bookings with status \"pending\" or \"confirmed\" and check_in date >= today).\n   614→\n   615→#### Test: Upcoming tab shows pending and confirmed future bookings\n   616→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with bookings: a confirmed booking checking in next week, a pending booking checking in next month, a completed booking from last month, and a cancelled booking.\n   617→- **Action:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab.\n   618→- **Expected:** Only the confirmed and pending future bookings are displayed. Completed and cancelled bookings are not shown in this tab.\n   619→\n   620→#### Test: Switching to Past tab shows completed bookings\n   621→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page with the \"Upcoming\" tab selected. The user has completed bookings.\n   622→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Past\" tab.\n   623→- **Expected:** The \"Past\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show only bookings with status \"completed\". Upcoming and cancelled bookings are not shown.\n   624→\n   625→#### Test: Switching to Cancelled tab shows cancelled bookings\n   626→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page with the \"Upcoming\" tab selected. The user has cancelled bookings.\n   627→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n   628→- **Expected:** The \"Cancelled\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show only bookings with status \"cancelled\". Upcoming and completed bookings are not shown.\n   629→\n   630→#### Test: Switching back to Upcoming tab from another tab\n   631→- **Initial state:** User is on the My Trips page with the \"Past\" tab selected.\n   632→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Upcoming\" tab.\n   633→- **Expected:** The \"Upcoming\" tab becomes selected/highlighted. The content area updates to show upcoming bookings again.\n   634→\n   635→#### Test: Tab shows empty state when no bookings exist for that category\n   636→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no completed bookings.\n   637→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Past\" tab.\n   638→- **Expected:** The \"Past\" tab content area displays a message like \"No past trips\" or \"You don't have any past trips yet.\" instead of an empty list.\n   639→\n   640→#### Test: Upcoming tab empty state message\n   641→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no pending or confirmed future bookings.\n   642→- **Action:** User views the \"Upcoming\" tab (default).\n   643→- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No upcoming trips\" with a suggestion to browse properties (e.g., a link to the home page).\n   644→\n   645→#### Test: Cancelled tab empty state message\n   646→- **Initial state:** User is logged in with no cancelled bookings.\n   647→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n   648→- **Expected:** The tab content area displays a message like \"No cancelled trips.\"\n   649→\n   650→#### Test: Tabs are functional on repeated use\n   651→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page.\n   652→- **Action:** User clicks \"Past\", then \"Cancelled\", then \"Upcoming\", then \"Past\" again.\n   653→- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected tab highlight and displays the correct set of bookings. The final state shows the \"Past\" tab selected with completed bookings displayed.\n   654→\n   655→### Component: TripCard\n   656→\n   657→#### Test: Trip card displays all required information\n   658→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. A booking exists for property \"Beach House\" in \"Malibu\" with check_in \"2026-05-01\", check_out \"2026-05-05\", status \"confirmed\", and total_price $800. The property has an image.\n   659→- **Expected:** The trip card displays: the property's main image, property title \"Beach House\", city \"Malibu\", dates \"May 1 – May 5, 2026\" (or similar formatted date range), a status badge showing \"Confirmed\" in green, and the total price \"$800\".\n   660→\n   661→#### Test: Trip card displays correct status badge colors\n   662→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. Bookings exist with different statuses.\n   663→- **Expected:** Status badges use the correct colors: \"Pending\" badge in yellow, \"Confirmed\" badge in green, \"Cancelled\" badge in red, \"Completed\" badge in blue.\n   664→\n   665→#### Test: Trip card shows property image or placeholder\n   666→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. One booking has a property with images, another has a property with no images.\n   667→- **Expected:** The trip card for the property with images shows the main property image. The trip card for the property without images shows a placeholder image.\n   668→\n   669→#### Test: Clicking trip card navigates to booking details\n   670→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the My Trips page. A trip card is displayed for a booking with id \"booking-123\".\n   671→- **Action:** User clicks on the trip card (not the cancel or review button).\n   672→- **Expected:** The app navigates to a booking detail view showing full booking information including property details, dates, guest count, price breakdown, and special requests.\n   673→\n   674→#### Test: Cancel button appears on pending bookings\n   675→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"pending\" is displayed.\n   676→- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button (or cancel icon button) that is clickable.\n   677→\n   678→#### Test: Cancel button appears on confirmed bookings\n   679→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n   680→- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Cancel\" button that is clickable.\n   681→\n   682→#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on completed bookings\n   683→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" is displayed.\n   684→- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n   685→\n   686→#### Test: Cancel button does not appear on already cancelled bookings\n   687→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Cancelled\" tab. A booking with status \"cancelled\" is displayed.\n   688→- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Cancel\" button.\n   689→\n   690→#### Test: Write Review button appears on completed bookings without a review\n   691→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A booking with status \"completed\" exists that does not have an associated review.\n   692→- **Expected:** The trip card shows a \"Write Review\" button that is clickable.\n   693→\n   694→#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on completed bookings that already have a review\n   695→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking exists that already has an associated review.\n   696→- **Expected:** The trip card does not show a \"Write Review\" button. Instead, it may show \"Reviewed\" text or a checkmark indicating a review was already submitted.\n   697→\n   698→#### Test: Clicking Write Review button navigates to review page\n   699→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Past\" tab. A completed booking with id \"booking-456\" has no review.\n   700→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Write Review\" button on that trip card.\n   701→- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/trips/booking-456/review` (the Write Review page).\n   702→\n   703→#### Test: Write Review button does not appear on pending, confirmed, or cancelled bookings\n   704→- **Initial state:** User is logged in. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"cancelled\".\n   705→- **Expected:** None of these trip cards display a \"Write Review\" button. The button only appears for \"completed\" bookings.\n   706→\n   707→#### Test: Trip cards are ordered by check-in date\n   708→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. Multiple upcoming bookings exist with different check-in dates.\n   709→- **Expected:** Trip cards are displayed in chronological order by check-in date, with the soonest upcoming trip first.\n   710→\n   711→### Component: CancelBookingDialog\n   712→\n   713→#### Test: Clicking Cancel button opens confirmation dialog\n   714→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the \"Upcoming\" tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed with a \"Cancel\" button.\n   715→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the trip card.\n   716→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog/modal appears asking the user to confirm the cancellation. The dialog displays text like \"Are you sure you want to cancel this booking?\" with the property name and dates for context. Two buttons are visible: \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") and \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\").\n   717→\n   718→#### Test: Confirming cancellation updates booking status to cancelled\n   719→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a confirmed booking.\n   720→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm Cancel\" (or \"Yes, Cancel\") button.\n   721→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab (or its status badge updates to \"Cancelled\" in red). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking cancelled successfully\"). The booking now appears in the \"Cancelled\" tab.\n   722→\n   723→#### Test: Dismissing cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n   724→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n   725→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Keep Booking\" (or \"No, Go Back\") button.\n   726→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking remains in its original status (pending). No API call is made. The trip card is unchanged.\n   727→\n   728→#### Test: Closing the dialog via overlay click keeps booking unchanged\n   729→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open.\n   730→- **Action:** User clicks outside the dialog (on the overlay/backdrop).\n   731→- **Expected:** The dialog closes without making any changes to the booking.\n   732→\n   733→#### Test: Cancel dialog shows property and date context\n   734→- **Initial state:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on a trip card for property \"Mountain Cabin\" with dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\".\n   735→- **Expected:** The confirmation dialog displays the property name \"Mountain Cabin\" and the booking dates \"June 10 – June 15, 2026\" so the user can confirm they are cancelling the correct booking.\n   736→\n   737→#### Test: After cancellation, booking moves from Upcoming to Cancelled tab\n   738→- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with a confirmed booking for \"Beach House\".\n   739→- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the \"Beach House\" trip card, then confirms the cancellation in the dialog.\n   740→- **Expected:** The \"Beach House\" trip card is removed from the \"Upcoming\" tab. User switches to the \"Cancelled\" tab and sees the \"Beach House\" booking with a red \"Cancelled\" status badge.\n   741→\n   742→#### Test: Cancel dialog is functional on repeated use\n   743→- **Initial state:** User is on the \"Upcoming\" tab with two cancellable bookings.\n   744→- **Action:** User clicks \"Cancel\" on the first booking, dismisses the dialog (clicks \"Keep Booking\"), then clicks \"Cancel\" on the second booking and confirms the cancellation.\n   745→- **Expected:** The first booking remains unchanged in the \"Upcoming\" tab. The second booking is cancelled and moves to the \"Cancelled\" tab. Each dialog open/close cycle works correctly.\n   746→\n   747→## Page: Host Dashboard (`/hosting`)\n   748→\n   749→<!-- Components: StatsOverview, ListingsTab, BookingsTab, AddListingForm -->\n   750→\n   751→### Component: StatsOverview\n   752→\n   753→#### Test: Host Dashboard requires login — redirects unauthenticated users\n   754→- **Initial state:** No user is logged in.\n   755→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   756→- **Expected:** The app redirects the user to `/login`. The Host Dashboard is not rendered.\n   757→\n   758→#### Test: Host Dashboard requires host status — shows upgrade prompt for non-hosts\n   759→- **Initial state:** A user is logged in with `is_host` set to false.\n   760→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   761→- **Expected:** The page displays a message indicating the user is not a host (e.g., \"You need to become a host to access this page\") with a link or button to navigate to their profile page (`/profile`) where they can become a host.\n   762→\n   763→#### Test: Stats overview displays total listings count\n   764→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 5 active properties and 1 inactive property in the database.\n   765→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   766→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Listings\" stat card showing \"5\" (only active listings counted). The card has a label \"Total Listings\" and a numeric value.\n   767→\n   768→#### Test: Stats overview displays active bookings count\n   769→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have 3 bookings with status \"confirmed\", 2 with status \"pending\", and 4 with status \"completed\".\n   770→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   771→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Active Bookings\" stat card showing \"5\" (pending + confirmed bookings). The card has a label \"Active Bookings\" and a numeric value.\n   772→\n   773→#### Test: Stats overview displays total earnings\n   774→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have completed bookings with total_price values of $500, $750, and $1200.\n   775→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   776→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays a \"Total Earnings\" stat card showing \"$2,450\" (sum of completed booking total prices). The value is formatted as currency.\n   777→\n   778→#### Test: Stats overview displays average rating\n   779→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have reviews with overall ratings of 4, 5, 3, and 5.\n   780→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   781→- **Expected:** The StatsOverview section displays an \"Average Rating\" stat card showing \"4.3\" (average of all review ratings, rounded to one decimal). A star icon is displayed next to the value.\n   782→\n   783→#### Test: Stats overview shows zeros for a new host with no data\n   784→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties, no bookings, and no reviews.\n   785→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   786→- **Expected:** All four stat cards display zero/empty values: \"Total Listings: 0\", \"Active Bookings: 0\", \"Total Earnings: $0\", and \"Average Rating: —\" (or \"N/A\" when no reviews exist).\n   787→\n   788→#### Test: Host Dashboard displays navigation tabs for Listings and Bookings\n   789→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n   790→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting`.\n   791→- **Expected:** Below the stats overview, two tabs are visible: \"Listings\" and \"Bookings\". The \"Listings\" tab is active/selected by default.\n   792→\n   793→#### Test: Switching between Listings and Bookings tabs\n   794→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host and on `/hosting` with the \"Listings\" tab active.\n   795→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n   796→- **Expected:** The Bookings tab content is displayed (table of bookings). The \"Bookings\" tab appears active/selected. User clicks \"Listings\" tab again and the listings grid is displayed.\n   797→\n   798→### Component: ListingsTab\n   799→\n   800→#### Test: Listings tab displays host's properties in a grid\n   801→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with 3 active properties: \"Beach House\" ($150/night), \"Mountain Cabin\" ($200/night), \"City Loft\" ($120/night).\n   802→- **Action:** User navigates to `/hosting` (Listings tab is active by default).\n   803→- **Expected:** A grid of 3 property cards is displayed. Each card shows the property title, main image, price per night, and status (active/inactive).\n   804→\n   805→#### Test: Listing card shows property details\n   806→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property: title \"Beach House\", price $150/night, city \"Malibu\", 4.5 average rating, 10 reviews, active status.\n   807→- **Expected:** The listing card displays the property title \"Beach House\", price \"$150/night\", location \"Malibu\", average rating \"4.5\" with star icon, review count \"10 reviews\", and a green \"Active\" badge.\n   808→\n   809→#### Test: Listing card has Edit button that navigates to property detail\n   810→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with a property (id \"prop-123\").\n   811→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Edit\" button on the property card.\n   812→- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/prop-123` where the host can view and edit their property details.\n   813→\n   814→#### Test: Listing card has Deactivate button for active properties\n   815→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an active property \"Beach House\".\n   816→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Deactivate\" button on the \"Beach House\" card.\n   817→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking \"Are you sure you want to deactivate this listing?\". The dialog shows the property name \"Beach House\".\n   818→\n   819→#### Test: Confirming deactivation sets property to inactive\n   820→- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n   821→- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button (e.g., \"Yes, Deactivate\").\n   822→- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/properties/:id` (which sets `is_active` to false). The dialog closes. The property card updates to show an \"Inactive\" status badge (gray or muted). A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Listing deactivated\"). The stats overview updates the \"Total Listings\" count to reflect the change.\n   823→\n   824→#### Test: Dismissing deactivation dialog keeps property active\n   825→- **Initial state:** The deactivation confirmation dialog is open for \"Beach House\".\n   826→- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss/cancel button.\n   827→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The property remains active with no changes.\n   828→\n   829→#### Test: Listing card shows Activate button for inactive properties\n   830→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with an inactive property \"Old Cabin\".\n   831→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Activate\" button on the \"Old Cabin\" card.\n   832→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/properties/:id` to set `is_active` to true. The property card updates to show a green \"Active\" badge. The \"Total Listings\" stat updates.\n   833→\n   834→#### Test: Listings tab shows empty state for host with no properties\n   835→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with no properties.\n   836→- **Expected:** The Listings tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"You don't have any listings yet\") and a prominent \"Add Listing\" button or call-to-action.\n   837→\n   838→#### Test: Add Listing button is visible on the Listings tab\n   839→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host.\n   840→- **Expected:** An \"Add Listing\" button is prominently displayed on the Listings tab (e.g., in the header area or as a floating action button). The button has clear text \"Add Listing\" or a \"+\" icon with label.\n   841→\n   842→#### Test: Deactivate and activate actions work on repeated use\n   843→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with two active properties.\n   844→- **Action:** User deactivates the first property (confirms dialog), then activates it again, then deactivates the second property.\n   845→- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct property's status. The stats overview correctly reflects the current count of active listings after each action.\n   846→\n   847→### Component: BookingsTab\n   848→\n   849→#### Test: Bookings tab displays table of bookings for host's properties\n   850→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. Their properties have bookings from various guests.\n   851→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n   852→- **Expected:** A table is displayed with columns: Property, Guest, Check-in, Check-out, Guests, Total, Status, and Actions. Each booking is a row in the table.\n   853→\n   854→#### Test: Bookings table shows correct data for each booking\n   855→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host. A booking exists: property \"Beach House\", guest \"Alice Smith\", check-in \"2026-07-01\", check-out \"2026-07-05\", 2 guests, total $750, status \"confirmed\".\n   856→- **Expected:** The table row displays: \"Beach House\", \"Alice Smith\", \"Jul 1, 2026\", \"Jul 5, 2026\", \"2\", \"$750\", a green \"Confirmed\" status badge.\n   857→\n   858→#### Test: Bookings tab has status filter controls\n   859→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab.\n   860→- **Expected:** Filter controls are visible above the table allowing the host to filter by status: \"All\", \"Pending\", \"Confirmed\", \"Cancelled\", \"Completed\". \"All\" is selected by default.\n   861→\n   862→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Pending status\n   863→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. Bookings exist with statuses \"pending\", \"confirmed\", and \"completed\".\n   864→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Pending\" status filter.\n   865→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"pending\" are displayed in the table. The \"Pending\" filter appears active/selected.\n   866→\n   867→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Confirmed status\n   868→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   869→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirmed\" status filter.\n   870→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"confirmed\" are shown. Other bookings are hidden.\n   871→\n   872→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Completed status\n   873→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   874→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Completed\" status filter.\n   875→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"completed\" are shown.\n   876→\n   877→#### Test: Filtering bookings by Cancelled status\n   878→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   879→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancelled\" status filter.\n   880→- **Expected:** Only bookings with status \"cancelled\" are shown.\n   881→\n   882→#### Test: Resetting filter to All shows all bookings\n   883→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with the \"Pending\" filter active.\n   884→- **Action:** User clicks the \"All\" filter.\n   885→- **Expected:** All bookings across all statuses are displayed again.\n   886→\n   887→#### Test: Status filters work on repeated use\n   888→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with various bookings.\n   889→- **Action:** User clicks \"Pending\", then \"Confirmed\", then \"All\", then \"Completed\".\n   890→- **Expected:** Each filter correctly shows the appropriate subset of bookings. The active filter indicator updates correctly each time.\n   891→\n   892→#### Test: Host can confirm a pending booking\n   893→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"pending\" for guest \"Bob\" at property \"Beach House\" is displayed.\n   894→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Confirm\" button on that booking row.\n   895→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"confirmed\". The booking's status badge changes from yellow \"Pending\" to green \"Confirmed\". The \"Confirm\" button is no longer visible for that booking. A success message is displayed (e.g., \"Booking confirmed\"). The \"Active Bookings\" stat in StatsOverview remains accurate.\n   896→\n   897→#### Test: Host can cancel a pending booking\n   898→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A pending booking is displayed.\n   899→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the pending booking row.\n   900→- **Expected:** A confirmation dialog appears asking the host to confirm cancellation. The dialog shows the guest name, property, and dates for context.\n   901→\n   902→#### Test: Confirming cancellation of a booking updates status\n   903→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a pending booking.\n   904→- **Action:** User clicks the confirm button in the dialog.\n   905→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The dialog closes. The booking's status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Cancel\" and \"Confirm\" action buttons are removed for that booking. A success message is displayed. The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases by 1.\n   906→\n   907→#### Test: Dismissing booking cancellation dialog keeps booking unchanged\n   908→- **Initial state:** The cancellation confirmation dialog is open for a booking.\n   909→- **Action:** User clicks the dismiss button or clicks outside the dialog.\n   910→- **Expected:** The dialog closes. The booking status remains unchanged.\n   911→\n   912→#### Test: Host can cancel a confirmed booking\n   913→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. A booking with status \"confirmed\" is displayed.\n   914→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cancel\" button on the confirmed booking row and confirms in the dialog.\n   915→- **Expected:** The app calls `PUT /api/bookings/:id` with status \"cancelled\". The status badge changes to red \"Cancelled\". The \"Active Bookings\" stat decreases.\n   916→\n   917→#### Test: Completed and cancelled bookings have no action buttons\n   918→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Bookings tab. Bookings exist with statuses \"completed\" and \"cancelled\".\n   919→- **Expected:** Booking rows with \"completed\" or \"cancelled\" status do not display \"Confirm\" or \"Cancel\" action buttons. Only pending and confirmed bookings show action buttons.\n   920→\n   921→#### Test: Bookings tab shows empty state when no bookings exist\n   922→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host with properties but no bookings.\n   923→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Bookings\" tab.\n   924→- **Expected:** The tab displays an empty state message (e.g., \"No bookings yet\").\n   925→\n   926→#### Test: Status badges display correct colors\n   927→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with bookings in all four statuses.\n   928→- **Expected:** Status badges use the correct colors: \"Pending\" has a yellow badge, \"Confirmed\" has a green badge, \"Cancelled\" has a red badge, \"Completed\" has a blue badge.\n   929→\n   930→#### Test: Confirm and cancel actions work on repeated use\n   931→- **Initial state:** User is on the Bookings tab with three pending bookings.\n   932→- **Action:** User confirms the first booking, cancels the second booking (confirming the dialog), and then confirms the third booking.\n   933→- **Expected:** Each action updates the correct booking. The first and third show \"Confirmed\" badges, the second shows \"Cancelled\". Stats update correctly after each action.\n   934→\n   935→### Component: AddListingForm\n   936→\n   937→#### Test: Clicking Add Listing button opens the multi-step form\n   938→- **Initial state:** User is logged in as a host on the Listings tab.\n   939→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Add Listing\" button.\n   940→- **Expected:** A multi-step form opens (modal or full-page). Step 1 is displayed with fields for property type and title. A step indicator shows progress (Step 1 of 7). \"Next\" and \"Cancel\" buttons are visible.\n   941→\n   942→#### Test: Step 1 — Property type selection and title input\n   943→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is open on Step 1.\n   944→- **Expected:** A dropdown or selection control lists property types: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". A text input field for the property title is visible. Both fields are required.\n   945→\n   946→#### Test: Step 1 — Selecting property type and entering title\n   947→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 1.\n   948→- **Action:** User selects \"Cabin\" from the property type selector and types \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\" in the title field.\n   949→- **Expected:** The property type shows \"Cabin\" selected. The title field displays \"Cozy Mountain Retreat\". The \"Next\" button becomes enabled (or was already enabled).\n   950→\n   951→#### Test: Step 1 — Validation prevents proceeding without required fields\n   952→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 1 with no selections made.\n   953→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" without selecting a property type or entering a title.\n   954→- **Expected:** Validation errors are displayed for both fields (e.g., \"Property type is required\", \"Title is required\"). The form does not advance to Step 2.\n   955→\n   956→#### Test: Step 2 — Location fields displayed\n   957→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 1 and clicked \"Next\".\n   958→- **Expected:** Step 2 is displayed with fields for: address (with geocoding/autocomplete), city, state, and country. A \"Back\" button and \"Next\" button are visible. The step indicator shows Step 2 of 7.\n   959→\n   960→#### Test: Step 2 — Address field uses autocomplete\n   961→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2.\n   962→- **Action:** User types \"123 Main\" in the address field.\n   963→- **Expected:** An autocomplete dropdown appears with address suggestions from a geocoding API (e.g., OpenStreetMap Nominatim). Selecting a suggestion populates the address field with the full address.\n   964→\n   965→#### Test: Step 2 — Address autocomplete populates related fields\n   966→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2.\n   967→- **Action:** User types in the address field and selects an autocomplete suggestion for \"123 Main St, Denver, CO, USA\".\n   968→- **Expected:** The address field is populated with \"123 Main St\". The city field is auto-filled with \"Denver\". The state field is auto-filled with \"CO\". The country field is auto-filled with \"USA\".\n   969→\n   970→#### Test: Step 2 — Validation requires city and country\n   971→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 2 with address filled but city and country empty.\n   972→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n   973→- **Expected:** Validation errors appear for city and country (e.g., \"City is required\", \"Country is required\"). The form does not advance.\n   974→\n   975→#### Test: Step 3 — Details fields displayed\n   976→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 2 and clicked \"Next\".\n   977→- **Expected:** Step 3 is displayed with numeric input fields for: max guests, bedrooms, beds, and bathrooms. Each field has increment/decrement controls or is a number input. The step indicator shows Step 3 of 7.\n   978→\n   979→#### Test: Step 3 — Setting property details\n   980→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 3.\n   981→- **Action:** User sets max guests to 4, bedrooms to 2, beds to 3, bathrooms to 1.\n   982→- **Expected:** All fields display the entered values. The \"Next\" button is enabled.\n   983→\n   984→#### Test: Step 3 — Validation requires all detail fields\n   985→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 3 with all fields at 0 or empty.\n   986→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\".\n   987→- **Expected:** Validation errors appear (e.g., \"Max guests must be at least 1\"). The form does not advance.\n   988→\n   989→#### Test: Step 4 — Amenities selection displayed\n   990→- **Initial state:** User completed Step 3 and clicked \"Next\".\n   991→- **Expected:** Step 4 is displayed with checkboxes for amenities grouped by category: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each category heading is visible with its amenities listed below. The step indicator shows Step 4 of 7.\n   992→\n   993→#### Test: Step 4 — Selecting amenities\n   994→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 4 with amenities loaded from `GET /api/amenities`.\n   995→- **Action:** User checks \"WiFi\" and \"Kitchen\" under Essentials, and \"Pool\" under Features.\n   996→- **Expected:** The selected amenities show as checked. The user can proceed to the next step. Amenities are optional (no validation error if none selected).\n   997→\n   998→#### Test: Step 4 — Amenities are toggleable\n   999→- **Initial state:** The Add Listing form is on Step 4 with \"WiFi\" already checked."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01BYZBEUEUZFsy2s9VeJe4VB","session_id":"bf64fb1f-6d22-482a-898e-953cd6c2617e","uuid":"b452ab55-79e3-4617-a888-512b6858988a"}
